# Deepcore — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Deepcore carries a debugging and automation surface, `window.__deepcore`, so an
expedition can be driven and inspected from code without touching a keyboard or
waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__deepcore` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it is
present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a reading, a pose of one value, or one of the controls below. A
pose sets one thing, and the game's own physics, drill, hazard, economy, and save
rules run from there exactly as they do in play, so a scenario driven from code
behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
